---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /
title: I build the evaluation systems that decide whether an AI answer is safe to ship
shortTitle: Libin Samkutty
description: Senior QA Automation Engineer building AI evaluation systems, golden datasets and production monitoring for a digital health platform across six country programs.
bodyClass: home
---
<section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero__inner">
        <div class="hero__content">
            <p class="hero__eyebrow">{{ site.title }} · {{ site.location.city }}, {{ site.location.country }}</p>

            <h1 class="hero__title">{{ site.tagline }}</h1>

            <p class="hero__lede">
                I am the only QA engineer on a digital health platform that answers questions about
                pregnancy, contraception and vaccination in seven languages across six countries.
                The interesting part of that job is not finding bugs. It is deciding, on evidence,
                whether a generated answer is good enough to send to someone who is worried about
                a symptom.
            </p>

            <p class="hero__actions">
                <a class="button button--primary" href="{{ '/work/' | url }}">Read the case studies</a>
                <a class="button button--ghost" href="{{ '/resume/' | url }}">Résumé</a>
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero__portrait">
            {# Replaced by the {% raw %}{% image %}{% endraw %} shortcode when the image pipeline lands.
               Alt is the person's name: a portrait's alt text is who it is, not a description of a suit. #}
            <img
                src="{{ '/assets/myphoto.png' | url }}"
                alt="{{ site.name }}"
                width="2048"
                height="1886"
                fetchpriority="high"
                decoding="async">
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="stat-rail" aria-labelledby="stat-rail-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="stat-rail-title">Evidence</h2>

        <dl class="stat-rail__list">
            <div class="stat">
                <dt class="stat__label">Golden-dataset cases gating every India Maternal Health release</dt>
                <dd class="stat__value">{% metric "golden_dataset_india_mh" %}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="stat">
                <dt class="stat__label">Cost of a full nightly evaluation run</dt>
                <dd class="stat__value">{% metric "nightly_eval_cost" %}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="stat">
                <dt class="stat__label">Prompt-regression review, per version</dt>
                <dd class="stat__value">{% metric "prompt_review_time" %}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="stat">
                <dt class="stat__label">Full CI regression suite</dt>
                <dd class="stat__value">{% metric "regression_suite_runtime" %}</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="stat stat--wide">
                <dt class="stat__label">What that covers</dt>
                <dd class="stat__value">{% metric "platform_scale" %}</dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="own-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="own-title">What I own</h2>

        <div class="grid grid--three">
            {% for item in projects.whatIOwn %}
            <div class="card card--plain" data-reveal>
                <h3 class="card__title">{{ item.title }}</h3>
                <p class="card__body">{{ item.body }}</p>
            </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

        {% architectureNote %}
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="work-title">Selected work</h2>

        <ul class="card-list">
            {% for item in collections.caseStudies %}
                {% if item.fileSlug in projects.featuredCaseStudies %}
                <li class="card card--case-study" data-reveal>
                    <p class="card__eyebrow">{{ item.data.period }}</p>
                    <h3 class="card__title">
                        <a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a>
                    </h3>
                    <p class="card__body">{{ item.data.description }}</p>
                </li>
                {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>

        <p class="section__more"><a href="{{ '/work/' | url }}">All work, including the systems that didn't warrant a case study</a></p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--emphasis" aria-labelledby="wrong-title">
    <div class="wrap wrap--measure">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="wrong-title">Things that didn't work</h2>

        <p>
            This section is not modesty. It is the fastest way to tell you what I am actually like
            to work with, and every case study on this site carries a section like it.
        </p>

        <div class="callout callout--limitation">
            <h3 class="callout__title">I built an evaluation system that could not fail</h3>
            <p>
                The platform's first LLM-as-a-judge used the same model family that had generated
                the answers it was grading. It scored well. It scored well because a model asked to
                grade its own reasoning agrees with itself. That is not an independent check. It is
                closer to a mirror.
            </p>
            <p><a href="{{ '/work/llm-judge-independence/' | url }}">How I found it and what replaced it</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="callout callout--limitation">
            <h3 class="callout__title">Four testing layers all missed the same gap</h3>
            <p>
                Golden-dataset regression, the conversational suite, retrieval faithfulness scoring
                and manual spot-checks were all green while a class of clinically important query
                was getting a sympathetic non-answer. Every layer was testing what we had thought to
                write down. None of them was reading what users were actually sending.
            </p>
            <p><a href="{{ '/work/production-evaluation-pipeline/' | url }}">What the production pipeline caught</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="callout callout--limitation">
            <h3 class="callout__title">I spent two years optimising a framework I then retired</h3>
            <p>
                Parallelisation, containerisation, flake reduction — real gains, all of them. Then
                the suite grew and the gains eroded, because the cost I kept optimising around was
                structural to the framework rather than to my configuration of it. Recognising that
                took longer than the migration did.
            </p>
            <p><a href="{{ '/work/from-robot-to-playwright/' | url }}">The diagnosis and the migration</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
    <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="writing-title">Latest writing</h2>

        <ul class="card-list card-list--posts">
            {% for item in collections.posts | limit(3) %}
            <li class="card card--post" data-reveal>
                <p class="card__eyebrow"><time datetime="{{ item.date | isoDate }}">{{ item.date | readableDate }}</time></p>
                <h3 class="card__title"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a></h3>
                <p class="card__body">{{ item.data.description }}</p>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>

        <p class="section__more"><a href="{{ '/writing/' | url }}">All writing</a></p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="oss-title">
    <div class="wrap wrap--measure">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="oss-title">Open source</h2>

        {% for project in skills.openSource %}
        <div class="card card--plain">
            <h3 class="card__title"><a href="{{ project.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ project.name }}</a></h3>
            <p class="card__body">{{ project.description }}</p>
            <p class="card__meta">{{ project.language }} · {{ project.license }} · {% metric project.metric %}</p>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
    <div class="wrap wrap--measure">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="timeline-title">Where I've been</h2>

        <ol class="timeline">
            {% for role in timeline.roles %}
            <li class="timeline__item{% if role.current %} timeline__item--current{% endif %}">
                <p class="timeline__period">
                    <time datetime="{{ role.start | isoDate }}">{{ role.start | monthYear }}</time>
                    –
                    {% if role.end %}<time datetime="{{ role.end | isoDate }}">{{ role.end | monthYear }}</time>{% else %}present{% endif %}
                </p>
                <h3 class="timeline__title">{{ role.title }}</h3>
                <p class="timeline__org">{{ role.employer }} · client {{ site.client.name }}</p>
            </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ol>

        <p class="section__more"><a href="{{ '/about/' | url }}">The longer version</a></p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--cta" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
    <div class="wrap wrap--measure">
        <h2 class="section__title" id="cta-title">Currently open to senior AI quality roles</h2>
        <p>
            {{ site.targetRoles | join(", ") }}. If you are building something where a wrong answer
            has a cost, that is the problem I want.
        </p>
        <p><a class="button button--primary" href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}">Get in touch</a></p>
    </div>
</section>
